            ('h2', 'Where to find it'),
            ('bullet', 'EtherApe window — on the toolbar, to the right of the timeline scrubber'),
            ('bullet', 'Web 3D view — bottom right, immediately right of the protocol legend'),
            ('h2', 'How it works'),
            ('p',  'It adds a pair of Windows Firewall block rules named NM_KILLSWITCH (one '
                   'inbound, one outbound, all profiles). Restoring the connection deletes them. '
                   'Nothing else is changed — your adapter, IP address and DNS settings are '
                   'left exactly as they were.'),
            ('bullet', 'Windows Firewall does not filter loopback, so the local dashboard on '
                       '127.0.0.1 keeps working while traffic is cut'),
            ('bullet', 'That means you can always re-enable from the same button you used to kill it'),
